adr: 0219
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: substring_empty
why: The fourth argument to the bounds check is the whole of AP 6.5.6 in the code generator -- it is what tells the runtime that the empty substring is admissible here. Passing a zero restores the standard's rule, which is the change reverted, and no diagnostic moves: a program that writes `s[i..i-1]` still compiles and simply stops when it reaches the statement. Only a case that *runs* one can tell. Re-anchored after ADR-0232, which made the argument a constant where it had been `if langStd = stdAfterschool`.
--- old
    write(ircode, ', i32 1');
--- new
    write(ircode, ', i32 0');
